    "groundContactBasis": "Inspected aerial picture confirms battered white bastions, terraced sea battery, open courts and stepped white governor blocks. Standard viewer PMTiles shows the coastal fort buildings and western castle parking. An approximate-.95rad heading and0.9horizontal plan scale fit the entrance toward that parking and sea-end batteries toward the coast. A reconstructed0.8m working rise keeps the court above coarse ground; wall/pier bottoms extend below sampled terrain and bridge deck approaches coarse ground at its outer end. Anchor -1.348211,5.08274; heading -0.95; standard PMTiles datum 10.98536388100999m. Floors are reconstructed and foundations extend below the coarse sampled ground.",
